# HOME COMING — response headers
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this automatically the moment you drop the
# folder in. On any other host it is simply ignored, which is harmless.
#
# Every header block below applies on top of this first one, so the security
# policy is written ONCE here. Do not repeat a "/*" block further down: every
# matching block is added to the response, and a browser that receives several
# Content-Security-Policy headers enforces all of them at once — the strictest
# wins, and fonts, Supabase and the script CDN silently stop working.
#
# - no page may be framed by another site, which stops clickjacking
# - no guessing of content types, which is a form-sniffing defence
# - the browser does not leak your page address when you follow a link out
# - after one visit, the browser refuses to ever try an unencrypted version
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the strict one, and it is only safe because
# the front end loads nothing it did not write itself. If you ever add a photo
# hosted somewhere else, add that domain to img-src below.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cumgwfrjilghykgszblt.supabase.co https://api.web3forms.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# The guest page. Always revalidated, so any edit you make shows up straight
# away while a repeat visit stays fast.

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The three front-end files. config.js is here on purpose: you will edit it,
# and it must not be served stale from a cache for long.

/Style.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/script.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/config.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# THE PRIVATE PANEL. Never cached, and never written into a browser history.
# This is the page with the phone numbers and email addresses in it.

/admin.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

/admin.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# The setup page. Not cached — you will keep coming back to it while you
# finish the job, and you do not want it to tell you a stale story.

/setup.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/setup.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Photographs and icons never change once you have put them there.

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# The service worker and the manifest. Never cached, so an update to the site
# actually reaches people instead of being pinned by a stale worker.

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

# Nothing should ever be listing the SQL, the notes, or the plain text files.

/supabase-schema.sql
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/fix-grants.sql
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/fix-trigger.sql
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/README.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
